{"tool_name":"rsrnasp","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rsrnasp","home":"https://github.com/Tan-group/rsRNASP","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A residue-separation-based statistical potential for RNA 3D structure evaluation.","addition_date":"2022-02-07T11:51:03.280574Z","last_update_date":"2022-02-07T11:51:03.283282Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:rsrnasp","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"wbzhang@whu.edu.cn","name":"Wenbing Zhang"},{"email":"zjtan@whu.edu.cn","name":"Zhi-Jie Tan"},{"name":"Xunxun Wang"},{"name":"Ya-Lan Tan"},{"name":"Ya-Zhou Shi"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"},{"term":"RNA structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2441"}]}],"name":"rsRNASP","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.bpj.2021.11.016","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 Biophysical SocietyKnowledge-based statistical potentials have been shown to be rather effective in protein 3-dimensional (3D) structure evaluation and prediction. Recently, several statistical potentials have been developed for RNA 3D structure evaluation, while their performances are either still at a low level for the test datasets from structure prediction models or dependent on the \u201cblack-box\u201d process through neural networks. In this work, we have developed an all-atom distance-dependent statistical potential based on residue separation for RNA 3D structure evaluation, namely rsRNASP, which is composed of short- and long-ranged potentials distinguished by residue separation. The extensive examinations against available RNA test datasets show that rsRNASP has apparently higher performance than the existing statistical potentials for the realistic test datasets with large RNAs from structure prediction models, including the newly released RNA-Puzzles dataset, and is comparable to the existing top statistical potentials for the test datasets with small RNAs or near-native decoys. In addition, rsRNASP is superior to RNA3DCNN, a recently developed scoring function through 3D convolutional neural networks. rsRNASP and the relevant databases are available to the public.","authors":[{"name":"Shi Y.-Z."},{"name":"Tan Y.-L."},{"name":"Tan Z.-J."},{"name":"Wang X."},{"name":"Zhang W."}],"date":"2022-01-04T00:00:00Z","journal":"Biophysical Journal","title":"rsRNASP: A residue-separation-based statistical potential for RNA 3D structure evaluation"},"pmcid":"PMC8758408","pmid":"34798137"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0097"},{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"rsRNASP","home":"https://bio.tools/rsrnasp","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A residue-separation-based statistical potential for RNA 3D structure evaluation.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:rsrnasp/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":false,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":25,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":4,"year":"2025"},{"count":5,"year":"2023"},{"count":6,"year":"2024"